      "text": "To begin, we first observe that\n\\[x^{2^n} = (x^{2^n})^2.\\]Thus, we can write our given series as\n\\[\\sum_{n = 0}^\\infty \\frac{x^{-2^n}}{x^2} = \\sum_{n = 0}^\\infty \\frac{1}{x^{2^n + 2}} ,\\]which is a geometric series with first term $(x^{2^0 + 2})^{-1} = 1/x^4$\nand common ratio $\\frac{1}{x^2}.$\nSince the sum of a geometric series is $\\frac{f}{1 - g},$ our completed expression is $\\frac{x^4}{1 - x^2}.$",
